   "id": "module-11-high-yield-formula-sheet-revision-traps-for-gate-2027",
   "title": "Module 11: High-Yield Formula Sheet & Revision Traps for GATE 2027",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "t": "h3",
     "text": "11.1 Master Formula Sheet"
    },
    {
     "t": "ol",
     "items": [
      "**Positional Weight:** $\\text{Value}(N)_{10} = \\sum_{i=-m}^{n-1} d_i \\cdot r^i$, with $0 \\le d_i \\le r - 1$.",
      "**Strict Base Bound:** $r \\ge \\max(d_i) + 1$.",
      "**Power-of-2 Shortcut:** $2^k \\iff k$ bits per digit ($8 = 2^3 \\implies 3$ bits, $16 = 2^4 \\implies 4$ bits).",
      "**Self-Complementing Condition:** $\\sum_{i=0}^3 w_i = 9$ (e.g., 2421, 5211, 8 4 -2 -1).",
      "**Binary to Gray:** $G_{n-1} = B_{n-1}$, $G_i = B_{i+1} \\oplus B_i$.",
      "**Gray to Binary:** $B_{n-1} = G_{n-1}$, $B_i = B_{i+1} \\oplus G_i$.",
      "**BCD Correction:** Add $+0110_2$ ($6_{10}$) if $\\text{Sum} > 9$ or $C_{out} = 1$.",
      "**Signed Complements Range:**"
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "ul",
     "items": [
      "SMR & 1's C: $[-(2^{n-1}-1), +(2^{n-1}-1)]$ (Dual zero).",
      "2's C: $[-2^{n-1}, +(2^{n-1}-1)]$ (Unique zero, asymmetric $-2^{n-1}$)."
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "ol",
     "items": [
      "**Overflow Hardware Flag:** $V = C_{in} \\oplus C_{out} = \\overline{A_{n-1}}\\,\\overline{B_{n-1}} S_{n-1} + A_{n-1} B_{n-1} \\overline{S_{n-1}}$.",
      "**Decimal Word Length Scaling:** $d > n \\log_{10} 2$."
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "h3",
     "text": "11.2 Top 5 GATE Traps to Avoid"
    },
    {
     "t": "alert",
     "type": "CAUTION",
     "text": "1. **The Padding Trap:** Never pad fractional bits on the left! Integer pads leading zeros on MSB; fraction pads trailing zeros on LSB.\n2. **The Base Identity Trap:** When solving base equations where $r$ cancels out (e.g., $5r+5 = 5r+5$), $r$ is not \"any real number\" \u2014 it is strictly constrained by physical digit symbols: $r > \\max(d_i)$.\n3. **The Carry vs. Overflow Trap:** $C_{out} = 1$ is for unsigned numbers; $V = 1$ is for signed numbers. $C_{out} = 1$ DOES NOT imply overflow.\n4. **The BCD vs. Binary Trap:** $(15)_{10} \\neq 1111_{\\text{BCD}}$. $(15)_{10} = 0001\\ 0101_{\\text{BCD}}$.\n5. **The Asymmetric Negation Trap:** In $n$-bit 2's complement, you CANNOT negate $-2^{n-1}$ into $+2^{n-1}$ within $n$ bits. Attempting to do so causes an arithmetic overflow!"
    }
   ]
